  "objective": "Audit commit 575e8a8f74da581298a8527f493e9eab8a45901f, focusing on changes since eb1333775e60fe191acfa5a420e9256feeb4a2b0. Read the original report: https://api.imd.fun/jobs/648ba2e5-46a0-4759-8439-73a6c9d81af6/report.md — not just the remediation summary. Reproduce and verify the same-UUID context-mismatch recovery, corrected quorum checks and assembled-body step-marker validation. Test unauthorized discard, fabricated owner context, genuine NotPassed verdict shopping, replay, retries and retained receipt history. Clearly distinguish enforced protections from owner-trust assumptions. Reproduce finding #4 exactly: Intake takes payment and invokes a callback inside request/requestWithFailure before returning, swallowing a callback revert. The new pre-payment revert test does not cover this. State whether it remains a live-compatibility blocker and what evidence would resolve it. Rerun the full regression suite, check payment caps/accounting and listing/ad escrow, remeasure worst-case callbacks against 200k gas, and verify deployed bytecode size against the contract-size limit. Separate material code blockers, documented owner powers and unverified live-protocol assumptions. No deployment, paid Intake request or fund movement.",
